                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]My playtime:[/b] 4.2h (based on steam, 100% achievement).\n[b]Grindy Achievement:[/b] No.\n[b]Optional Achievement:[/b] Yes (12 achievements).\n[b]Difficult Achievement:[/b] No (well, there are 2 which are quite hard though).\n[b]Developer Response:[/b] No (last response is in 8 Mar, 2017).\n\n[h1]Intro[/h1]\nBetween Me and The Night is an adventure game about a boy with his game. There isn't much text in the story so you need to interpret the story by yourself.\n\n[h1]Graphics[/h1]\nThe game is using a simple yet beautiful 2D graphics. Some cutscenes have graphics that look like 3D. There are usually some animation of people in the events and those looks great.\n\n[h1]Music[/h1]\nI hardly hear any music in the game but whenever i hear one, it sounds relaxing. The sfx also works well with the bgm. All in all, the music is pleasant to hear.\n\n[h1]Story[/h1]\nAs i said before, there isn't much text in the story. You'll have to interpret the story by yourself from the events and cutscenes. However, some cutscenes are very laggy (i even didn't see all of the final cutscenes because the cutscene stuck which makes me have to skip it). I don't know whether it's just me or not, but i hardly understand the story [spoiler]except the fact that the boy is running away from his problems by playing games[/spoiler].\n\n[h1]The game[/h1]\nThe game will start with a simple tutorial for the controls and then moved to the main story. In the main story itself, you are placed in your bedroom without any idea of what to do, except by following the \"flashy lights\" or exploring all rooms for hints. This happened all the way until the game ends which can make it hard if you don't really pay attention to the details. You can take almost all items in the game (up to 6 items at once). You also might take any useless items that way.\n\nYou might think that you'd rather to explore all rooms for hints to make it easier. However, in the very first level, the developer added a nasty ghost enemy which will kill you whenever you are close to it. This also can happen if you have a bad luck and encountering it in the place where you came out. You'll return to your bedroom if you got \"hit\" by them (keeping all of your items).\n\nThere are also some \"boss\" that you have to fight or avoid. It's usually requires a simple task such as running away and it shouldn't pose much problem (unless if you're that unlucky). These nasty enemies can only be encountered at the first level, which makes the first level to be the hardest level out there (while the last level is the easiest).\n\nThere are also some minigames throughout the game (and some are mandatory). These mini games have a very bad control that can make you spend more time than needed in order to get the achievements. The worse thing is, you have to beat one minigame which has a very slow walking speed in order to beat the game.\n\nLastly, there is no manual save. The game will automatically save for each level and you can load any level after you finished the game from the main menu.\n\nPros:\n- Beautiful graphics\n- Mini games\n\nCons:\n- Bad mini game controls\n- \"Laggy\" cutscenes\n- No manual save\n\n[h1]Conclusion[/h1]\nThis is an adventure game where you have to interpret the story yourself. The story requires you to play minigames with bad controls.\n\n[h1]Should you buy this game?[/h1]\n[b]No.[/b]\n[i]I don't think i'm enjoying myself when i played this game. I hardly know what to do and the minigames aren't fun at all. You even have to finish one mini game to finish the game.[/i]",
